{"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Tries"}],"title":"Tries","symbolKind":"module","roleHeading":"Framework","externalID":"Tries","role":"collection"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie"},{"text":" is a set of sequences and a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/TrieDictionary"},{"text":" a dictionary keyed by them, both kept in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a trie (Fredkin, 1960): a tree whose edges carry symbols and whose root-to-vertex paths spell the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"keys. They answer the queries a hash set cannot: every key with a prefix","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"elements(withPrefix:)"},{"text":", whose ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"count"},{"text":" is O(1)), whether any key has one (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hasPrefix(_:)"},{"text":"), and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the longest key that is a prefix of a query (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"longestPrefix(of:)"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]},{"code":["import Tries","","let words = Trie([\"car\", \"cart\", \"cat\", \"dog\"])","words.contains(\"cat\")                                   \/\/ true","words.elements(withPrefix: \"car\").map { String($0) }    \/\/ [\"car\", \"cart\"]","words.longestPrefix(of: \"carton\").map { String($0) }    \/\/ \"cart\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Keys are any sequence of the symbol type and are stored as ","type":"text"},{"code":"[Symbol]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". For text, the symbol","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"type decides what a step is: ","type":"text"},{"code":"Trie<Character>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" steps by grapheme cluster, ","type":"text"},{"code":"Trie<Unicode.Scalar>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"by scalar, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Trie<UInt8>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" over ","type":"text"},{"code":"utf8","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" by byte, the fastest of the three, because comparing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"bytes is cheaper than comparing ","type":"text"},{"code":"Character","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s. When the symbols are ","type":"text"},{"code":"Comparable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", each vertex keeps","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its children sorted, so iteration is in lexicographic order; otherwise children come in the order","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"they were added.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTreeDictionary","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" hold the same keys and answer the same queries,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with the same names, in a radix tree (Morrison, 1968): every chain of vertices with one child and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"no key is merged into one edge labelled with all its symbols, so there is a vertex per key and per"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"branching point rather than per symbol. They suit keys with long shared prefixes, such as file"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"paths or URLs, and build faster and in less memory than a trie of the same keys."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A trie’s shape converts to Grafluent’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PrefixTree"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PrefixTree(_:)"},{"text":", and a radix tree’s to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Arborescence"},{"text":" of its vertices’ prefixes with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Arborescence(_:)"},{"text":" (import Grafluent’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trees"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"module beside this one).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" (Aho and Corasick, 1975) finds every occurrence of any of a set of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patterns in one pass over a text, in O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":" + "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"z"}]},{"type":"text","text":") for "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" symbols and "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"z"}]},{"type":"text","text":" matches: a trie of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patterns with failure links. Its "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/statesView-swift.property","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is the automaton as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"code":["let automaton = AhoCorasickAutomaton(patterns: [\"he\", \"she\", \"his\", \"hers\"])","automaton.matches(in: \"ushers\").map(\\.patternIndex)   \/\/ [1, 0, 3]"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"topicSections":[{